{"level":"error","message":"AI returned invalid JSON in generateProblem","raw":"{\n  \"title\": \"Optimal Path in a Grid with Obstacles and Teleporters\",\n  \"slug\": \"optimal-path-grid-obstacles-teleporters\",\n  \"description\": \"You are given a grid of size `N x M` where each cell can either be empty (`0`), an obstacle (`1`), or a teleporter (`T`). A teleporter instantly moves you to another specified cell in the grid. Your task is to find the shortest path from the top-left corner `(0, 0)` to the bottom-right corner `(N-1, M-1)`. If it's impossible to reach the destination, return `-1`.\n\n  The grid is represented as a 2D array of strings, where each string represents a row in the grid. Each character in the string can be one of the following:\n  - `0`: An empty cell.\n  - `1`: An obstacle.\n  - `T`: A teleporter. Each teleporter is uniquely identified by a lowercase letter (`a-z`). There will be exactly two cells with the same identifier, representing the start and end points of the teleporter.\n\n  You can move up, down, left, or right to adjacent cells, but not diagonally. Moving through a teleporter counts as a single step.\n\n  Constraints:\n  - `2 <= N, M <= 100`\n  - `grid[i][j]` is either `0`, `1`, or `T`.\n  - There will be at most 26 teleporters in the grid.\n  - The starting cell `(0, 0)` and the ending cell `(N-1, M-1)` will always be empty cells.\n\n  Example 1:\n  Input: grid = [\\\"00T\\\", \\\"010\\\", \\\"000\\\"]\n  Output: 3\n  Explanation: The optimal path is (0,0) -> (0,2) -> (2,2). The teleporter at (0,2) moves you to (2,2).\n\n  Example 2:\n  Input: grid = [\\\"010\\\", \\\"010\\\", \\\"000\\\"]\n  Output: 4\n  Explanation: The optimal path is (0,0) -> (1,0) -> (2,0) -> (2,1) -> (2,2).\n\n  Example 3:\n  Input: grid = [\\\"010\\\", \\\"011\\\", \\\"010\\\"]\n  Output: -1\n  Explanation: It is impossible to reach the bottom-right corner.\",\n  \"referenceSolution\": \"function shortestPath(grid: string[]): number {\n    const N = grid.length;\n    const M = grid[0].length;\n    const directions = [[0, 1], [1, 0], [0, -1], [-1, 0]];\n    const visited = new Set<string>();\n    const queue = [{ x: 0, y: 0, steps: 0 }];\n    const teleporters = new Map<string, { x: number; y: number }>();\n\n    for (let i = 0; i < N; i++) {\n        for (let j = 0; j < M; j++) {\n            if (grid[i][j] !== '0' && grid[i][j] !== '1') {\n                if (!teleporters.has(grid[i][j])) {\n                    teleporters.set(grid[i][j], { x: i, y: j });\n                } else {\n                    const [x, y] = [teleporters.get(grid[i][j]).x, teleporters.get(grid[i][j]).y];\n                    teleporters.set(grid[i][j], { x, y, targetX: i, targetY: j });\n                    teleporters.set(`${i},${j}`, { x, y, targetX: x, targetY: y });\n                }\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    while (queue.length > 0) {\n        const { x, y, steps } = queue.shift()!;\n        const key = `${x},${y}`;\n\n        if (visited.has(key)) continue;\n        visited.add(key);\n\n        if (x === N - 1 && y === M - 1) return steps;\n\n        for (const [dx, dy] of directions) {\n            const nx = x + dx;\n            c...","service":"code-execution-backend api","timestamp":"2026-04-06T16:21:43.298Z"}
